# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
bin/
dist/

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local sqlite databases
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Playwright MCP output (screenshots, traces, session state)
.playwright-mcp/
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
node_modules/

# Agent Manager worktrees are ephemeral checkouts, never part of the repo
.opencode/worktrees/

# Toolchain binaries installed by the Makefile (tailwind, templ). Never
# committed: the standalone Tailwind binary is ~110MB.
#
# No trailing slash, and that is load-bearing rather than cosmetic. A trailing
# slash makes the pattern match directories only, so a *symlink* named .toolbin is
# not ignored — which is exactly what a worktree that links its tool directory to
# the primary checkout contains. That symlink then lands in a diff, and on a CI
# runner `go install` fails with "mkdir .toolbin/: file exists" because the path
# is a symlink rather than a directory. Phase 4 committed one exactly that way.
.toolbin

# Generated frontend assets. Produced by `make css` and `make templ`, which
# `make check` runs before `go build` because internal/web embeds them. A
# generated file in a diff means the gate was not run.
internal/web/static/dist/
*_templ.go

# Hugo build output and cache
docs/public/
docs/resources/
docs/.site-check/
docs/.hugo_build.lock
# Design records staged from .opencode/plans by `make site-plans`
docs/assets/plans/

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/
*.code-workspace
